add('daycare.html', {
  path:'/daycare', title:'Doggy Daycare In Bayers Lake', description:'Learn about supervised doggy daycare at Jollytails Resort, including playgroups, assessments, requirements, hours, and booking.',
  body: hero({kicker:'Doggy Daycare',title:'A full day of play, friends, and fun.',copy:'Our supervised daycare gives social dogs space to move between indoor and outdoor play areas, rest when they need it, and enjoy a group chosen with their comfort in mind.',image:img.daycare,alt:'A group of dogs playing together on the Resort outdoor turf',actionsClass:'equal-action-buttons',actions:[requestButton('/daycare/assessment','New Clients: Request Assessment'),reservationButton(portal,'Existing Clients: Book Daycare','target="_blank" rel="noopener"')]}) +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${cards([
    {mark:'In + out',title:'Space For Real Play',copy:'Dogs enjoy climate-controlled indoor space and outdoor turf, with pools added when the weather cooperates.'},
    {mark:'Right fit',title:'Thoughtful Playgroups',copy:'Dogs are generally grouped by size and play style. Little dogs have their own dedicated indoor and outdoor area.'},
    {mark:'Daily',title:'A Day You Can Follow',copy:'Our team supervises play and sends an emailed report card so you can see how your dog’s day went.'}
  ])}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${split({image:img.pool,alt:'Three golden retrievers cooling off in a pool in the Resort outdoor play yard',kicker:'The Daycare Experience',title:'A tired dog is a happy dog.',body:'<p>Doggy Daycare is a service for dog owners who are away during the day, or who just need a little help providing extra activity and socialization for their best friends. Jollytails focuses on a fun and safe environment for dogs to meet new friends, burn off some energy, and maybe even learn a few tricks along the way.</p><p>Jollytails provides a supervised place for pets to exercise and play. Our spacious facility allows dogs the freedom to interact with other pets and people, cool off in the pools, or just relax and enjoy the fun. Dog daycare is a great way to relax your pet. Exercise and socialization can curb undesirable boredom-driven behaviors such as destruction and incessant barking. Dogs, much like people, can become frustrated and a little “shack-whacky” when they don’t get the exercise and stimulation they need.</p><p>Unlike dog parks and pet-sitting in the home, doggy day care ensures a consistent, fully supervised way to alleviate boredom, stimulate and socialize pets so they are more relaxed and content at home with you (which means that you are more relaxed and content too!). Our goal is to send your dog home tired and happy!</p>'})}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container">${sectionHead('A Day At Daycare','Play, pause, and plenty of choice.','Every visit is shaped around the dogs attending that day, but the general rhythm includes active play and quieter moments.',true)}<ol class="steps-grid"><li><span>1</span><h3>Arrive And Settle In</h3><p>Your dog joins an appropriate playgroup and gets time to settle into the space and the day.</p></li><li><span>2</span><h3>Play And Explore</h3><p>Supervised indoor and outdoor play gives dogs room to socialize, move, cool off, or take a break.</p></li><li><span>3</span><h3>Eat, Rest, And Rejoin</h3><p>Dogs with food from home eat separately and rest to digest before returning to play. The day finishes at each dog’s own pace.</p></li></ol></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Inside And Out','A facility designed for active play and real rest.','',true)}<div class="inside-out-layout"><div class="split-photo inside-out-photo"><img src="${img.indoorDaycare}" alt="Dogs relaxing together in the spacious indoor daycare play area at Jollytails Resort" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="inside-out-primary"><p>Our facilities provide a generous indoor and outdoor play space. The entire outdoor areas are covered in a soft, thick, high quality artificial turf, both highly drainable and durable. This gives the look and feel of grass (along with the comfort!). This allows dogs to use the bathroom outside on grass rather than being forced to go inside. Plus, our dogs love to take a little play break and have an outdoor snooze on the turf, either in the shade or the sun.</p><p>Our indoor surface is sealed with an increased-tread epoxy flooring. In addition to providing great traction for play time, this surface allows us to fully clean after each day and wash everything down our built in floor drain. No bacteria to get caught in tiling or between cracks! In addition, we have several anti-fatigue mats and cot beds for dogs to rest on when they are tired.</p></div><div class="inside-out-secondary"><div><p>Outdoor turf is cleaned and pressure washed daily. Indoor is vacuumed, mopped and drained daily as well. We take cleanliness very seriously!</p><p>Our guests spend the vast majority of their time relaxing in our huge open play area – we only confine dogs temporarily so they can eat and digest fully in peace!</p></div><div><p>Jollytails staff are highly experienced and go through a continued training process that enables them to understand dog language and play styles, which enables them to respond effectively to signals and behaviours before play escalates. Owners are kept fully aware of how their dogs enjoyed their day with a daily report by email each day their dog attends Jollytails.</p></div></div></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container">${sectionHead('The Jollytails Difference','We believe we are the safest and most fun daycare in town!','Jollytails strives to create a positive, stress-free play environment for all our guests. We are unique from other daycares for the following reasons:',true)}<div class="narrow-panel">${list(['We strongly recommend bringing food for your dog(s) at lunch time. Dogs are crepuscular animals (active at dawn and dusk) and naturally want to rest during the afternoon. Allowing them alone time with food greatly reduces stress and keeps their energy levels up. Along with top Canadian-made brands of kibble and raw, we also offer a delectable selection of Yappy Hour lunchtime treats! Our retail staff can talk to you about the food that is right for your dog. A hungry dog is an unhappy dog!','Our dogs are assessed and accepted carefully. We have a zero-tolerance policy for aggressive dogs and some dogs may even be refused an assessment based on their history and intake form.','We have SPACE! The American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals recommends 75-100 square feet per dog in a daycare facility. Our facilities have plenty of space and we keep our numbers well below the 100sqft/dog recommendation. Dogs are allowed to naturally use the bathroom outside at all times and have space to run and play without being stuck in a crowded room. Overcrowding leads to fighting and stress.','We are honest and upfront on your dog’s behaviour. We provide daily report cards to your email and will discuss any concerns we have with you. Training plans can be recommended where required.'])}</div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('How To Become A Jollytails Resort Guest','Daycare requirements.')}<p>To stay and play at Jollytails Resort, dogs must be over 16 weeks of age and spayed/neutered (if at least 6 months old). You must provide proof of core vaccines (DHPP - Distemper, Hepatitis, Parvovirus and Parainfluenza) as well as Rabies, Leptospirosis, and Bordetella (canine cough). Your dog must be flea and tick free and must pass our assessment interview. Dogs in daycare must wear a regular, quick release collar free of dog tags, activity trackers and airtags.</p><a class="text-link" href="/requirements">Read complete guest requirements →</a></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">A good routine</p><h2>Regular attendance helps.</h2><p>Please note: Customers who do not attend daycare during a period of three months may be subject to a re-assessment process. We recommend dogs attend daycare at a minimum of once bi-weekly to fully enjoy daycare.</p></aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Health At Daycare','Understanding kennel cough.')}<p>“Kennel cough” is a common name for a group of contagious respiratory illnesses that can spread anywhere dogs gather, including daycare, boarding, grooming facilities, parks, and veterinary clinics.</p><p>Vaccination helps protect dogs and can reduce the severity of illness, but it cannot prevent every cause of kennel cough. Even with vaccination, daily cleaning, and health screening, group environments cannot eliminate every exposure risk.</p><p>Keep your dog home if you notice coughing, gagging, sneezing, nasal discharge, unusual tiredness, poor appetite, or other signs of illness. Please also let the Resort know about a suspected or confirmed contagious illness.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Peace Of Mind</p><h2>Why consider pet insurance?</h2><p>Daycare is an active social environment. Our team prioritizes safety, but minor scratches or play-related injuries can occasionally happen, and veterinary care can be costly.</p><p>Pet insurance may help with unexpected expenses. Jollytails Resort is not affiliated with an insurer, so compare coverage, exclusions, waiting periods, and limits directly with providers.</p></aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Your First Visit','Assessment.')}<div class="narrow-panel"><p>When you first contact Jollytails Resort you will be asked to fill out our detailed assessment form which gathers history and information on your dog. If we believe your dog is a good fit for daycare based on the form, we will then schedule an interview where you and your dog will meet our staff and some of our staff dogs.</p><p>If all initial meetings go well, your dog will be introduced to one of our playgroups. If your dog is successful, you can leave your dog for a half day. At the end of their day we will let you know how your dog enjoyed playing and meeting all the other dogs. After that, you’re welcome to come back anytime! Owners should plan to stay for up to 30 minutes to ensure their dog enjoys the playgroup. If at any point the dog is deemed unacceptable, owners will be asked to leave with their dog.</p><p>Please note that your assessment day is charged at the regular half day rate.</p></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container faq-layout"><div>${sectionHead('Daycare FAQs','Good to know before drop-off.')}</div>${faq([
    {q:'What will my dog do at Jollytails Resort?',html:`<p>Dogs at Jollytails Resort enjoy interacting with our staff and all the other dogs in our fabulous indoor and outdoor play areas. We believe in providing a large amount of space for dogs so they don’t feel cramped or restricted. Our two large doors allow dogs to come and go from both the indoor and outdoor play areas with lots of interesting things to interact with including pools, shaded areas, resting mats, and of course, our staff and other dogs!</p>`},
    {q:'What should I bring?',html:`<p>Dogs need to wear a regular quick release collar free of any tags. No harnesses or choke/prong or e-collars please! If you want your dog to have an afternoon meal, please bring it with you. We highly recommend dogs be fed some food during a full day stay.</p>`},
    {q:'When can I drop off and pick up my dog?',html:`<p>Our doggy daycare hours can be viewed at the very bottom of this page.</p><p>Please indicate on your reservation what time you plan to drop off your dog. We offer both full day and half day rates. Half days can be mornings or afternoons, but dogs cannot be dropped off any later than 1pm.</p>`},
    {q:'How do I reserve a spot?',html:`<p>Once you’re approved for daycare, you will be given instructions to access our online reservation system where you can see your booking history, make/cancel reservations and more. Daycare tends to fill up quickly, so reservations are strongly recommended. Unfortunately, we may have to turn away clients who arrive without a reservation if there isn’t room on that day.</p>`},
    {q:'When will my dog eat?',html:`<p>If you provide a meal or select one of our Yappy Hour lunchtime treats, we will separate your dog out into a private kennel or crate in order to have their lunch. We allow them a chance to rest privately before returning to the play area to prevent <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastric_dilatation_volvulus">bloat</a>. The duration of rest will depend upon the dog’s risk for bloat. We use slow feed bowls and will not feed more than 1 cup of food at a time to minimize risk.</p><p>We do not provide food for the dog since providing a different brand of food may upset your dog’s stomach and cause diarrhea. It is not mandatory to provide food but it is recommended to keep up the dog’s energy! It is also recommended to feed a high quality food for active dogs - we can help you choose a great diet for your pet.</p><p>Please label your dog’s meal with their name and feeding instructions, and do not bring it in a glass container.</p>`},
    {q:'Should I feed my dog prior to drop-off?',html:`<p>We suggest that you feed our dog at least one hour before coming to minimize risk of vomiting and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastric_dilatation_volvulus">bloat.</a> If your dog has just eaten upon arrival, we will place them in a kennel to allow their stomach to settle before playing.</p>`},
    {q:'What if my dog gets sick or injured?',html:`<p>Our first priority is the health and safety of your dog. If at any time our staff feel that your dog requires emergency veterinary care, we will contact you. If we are unable to reach you or your emergency contact, or if your dog appears to be in immediate distress, we will bring your dog to a veterinary hospital for treatment.</p>`},
    {q:'Do dogs ever get hurt?',html:`<p>During normal play its common for dogs to get scratches or minor injuries during play, and while we do our best to monitor all dogs it is possible for more serious injuries to occur. However, this is rare. We are proud of our expertise in dog behaviour, as our facility is not only a daycare but also a training and behaviour rehabilitation centre for dogs. We manage behaviour and play so that aggression issues do not happen.</p><p>In the event of any emergency that requires immediate attention, owners will be contacted, and if required, your dog will be brought to the nearest vet for treatment. Safety and health are our top priority.</p><p>Aggression which causes damage to a dog is not tolerated at Jollytails and any dog causing damage will be immediately banned from Jollytails.</p><p>Pet insurance is recommended for any dogs that play in groups or attend dog parks, as even minor injuries can be costly.</p>`},
    {q:'If my dog is sick or injured, can they come to daycare?',html:`<p>Dogs who are sick, whether contagious or not, should stay home and other arrangements for care should be found. Daycare is for healthy dogs to play and have fun.</p>`},
    {q:'What is kennel cough?',html:`<p>If your dog exhibits a sudden dry hacking cough or retching sound, he may be experiencing a condition referred to as kennel cough (Bordetella). Kennel cough is a common upper respiratory infection, comparable to a human cold. Due to its contagious nature, you should refrain from exposing other dogs to your pet if they are showing symptoms. For more information, visit <a href="http://healthypets.mercola.com/">http://healthypets.mercola.com/</a>.</p>`},
    {q:'Will my dog like Jollytails?',html:`<p>If your dog likes to play with other dogs, then absolutely! Part of our detailed assessment is to determine if your dog will like our environment and play areas. We are very honest and if we feel your dog is not enjoying themselves, we will let you know. If your dog doesn’t like other dogs or is very shy, they may not like Jollytails, but unlike other daycares, we can provide behaviour training and advice on how to help you. Please chat with us about your dog so we can give you the best advice.</p>`},
    {q:'If my dog is currently a client at another Jollytails locations, do I need to provide a new assessment form?',html:`<p>Yes. Jollytails Resort does not share access to client information with other Jollytails locations. We do require a new submission of your assessment form which will enable us to create your account at Jollytails Resort, and will help us get to know your dog. The next assessment steps will be determined on a case by case basis.</p>`},
    {q:'Are daycare credits transferable between Jollytails Resort and other Jollytails locations?',html:`<p>Jollytails Resort does not have access to customer packages or loyalty information from other Jollytails locations. However, all package discounts and loyalty programs are still available to be purchased from Jollytails Resort.</p>`},
    {q:'How are your play groups arranged?',html:`<p>We have two separate indoor and outdoor playspaces. Dogs are generally divided by size, though there are sometimes exceptions. For example, we have seen smaller dogs that love to romp in the regular area, whereas more timid medium dogs sometimes do best in the small dog area. We evaluate each dog individually and assign them the play area that suits them best.</p>`},
    {q:'Should I bring toys for my dog?',html:`<p>No, there will be some fun objects to interact with including several pools. With smaller toys, dogs may defend or guard objects that are in their “mouth area”, but dogs tend not to do this with larger sized objects – especially if many similar items are available to play with.</p>`},
    {q:'Can my dog be groomed while in daycare?',html:`<p>We can accommodate baths, nail trims and more during your pup’s daycare day! Our incredible groomers tend to book up quickly, and may not be able to accommodate full grooming services same-day. Please contact us to ask about availability for grooming during daycare!</p>`}
  ])}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container narrow-panel centered-heading"><p class="section-kicker">Stay In The Loop</p><h2>Sign Up for our Jollytails Newsletter</h2><p><a class="button button-primary" href="/#newsletter">Sign Up</a></p><p class="small-note">We respect your privacy.</p></div></section>` +
  cta('Ready for daycare?','New dogs start with an assessment. Approved clients can reserve through the existing daycare portal.',[requestButton('/daycare/assessment','Request An Assessment'),reservationButton(portal,'Book Daycare','target="_blank" rel="noopener"')])
});

add('boarding.html', {
  path:'/boarding', title:'Overnight Dog Boarding In Halifax', description:'Plan an overnight boarding stay at Jollytails Resort with supervised social play, private sleeping spaces, and 24-hour on-site care.',
  body: hero({kicker:'Overnight Boarding',title:'Play all day. Rest easy all night.',copy:'Boarding at Jollytails Resort combines supervised social days, a sleeping space chosen for your dog, and a team member on site 24 hours a day.',image:img.boardingRest,alt:'Three dogs resting together on an elevated bed at Jollytails Resort',position:'50% 50%',actionsClass:'equal-action-buttons',actions:[requestButton('/reservations/boarding/new','New Guest Boarding Request'),reservationButton('/reservations/boarding/existing','Returning Guest Booking')]}) +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${cards([
    {mark:'24/7',title:'Someone Is Always On Site',copy:'A team member remains at the facility around the clock while overnight guests are staying with us.'},
    {mark:'Private',title:'A Space Of Their Own',copy:'Dogs sleep in a private kennel or crate selected for their size, comfort, and usual sleeping routine.'},
    {mark:'Social',title:'Daycare Is Included',copy:'Eligible boarding guests join supervised daycare during their stay, including arrival day and departure day until 2pm.'}
  ])}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${split({image:img.play,alt:'Dogs playing outdoors in the Resort daycare yard',kicker:'A Resort Stay',title:'A familiar rhythm from daytime to bedtime.',body:'<p>Boarding is designed for social dogs who are comfortable in group daycare. Days include indoor and outdoor play, rest, feeding, and individual attention. At night, each guest settles into a private sleeping space.</p><p>Daily email report cards help you stay connected while your dog is with us.</p>'})}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Pack For A Comfortable Stay','What to bring.')}${list(['Your dog’s regular food, with enough for the full stay.','A familiar bed or blanket.','Favourite toys, bones, or safe chews.','Clearly labelled medication and instructions, after confirming the team can administer it.'])}<p class="small-note">Please leave dishes and electronic toys at home. Refrigerated and frozen food can be stored at the Resort.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Timing</p><h2>Check in before 1pm.</h2><p>Boarding guests check in before 1pm so they have time to settle into the day. Checkout is by 2pm; daycare fees apply after 2pm.</p><a class="text-link" href="/prices#boarding-policies">Deposits And Cancellations →</a></aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Included In The Nightly Rate',"A breakdown of what’s included in your overnight boarding rate.",'Daytime play, overnight supervision, and the everyday essentials are all part of your dog’s stay.',true)}${cards([
    {mark:'24/7',title:'On-Site Overnight Care',copy:'A trained team member remains on site 24 hours a day while boarding guests are staying at the Resort.'},
    {mark:'Play',title:'Daycare Throughout The Stay',copy:'The rate includes daycare on check-in day, every full day of the stay, and on departure day until 2pm.'},
    {mark:'Sleep',title:'A Sleeping Space Chosen For Your Dog',copy:'The team selects a kennel or crate based on your dog’s size, comfort, and usual sleeping routine. A blanket and fresh water are provided in the climate-controlled facility.'},
    {mark:'Meals',title:'Food Prepared As Directed',copy:'Bring your dog’s regular food—raw, frozen, kibble, or fresh—and the team will prepare and serve it according to your instructions.'},
    {mark:'Care',title:'Feeding And Most Medications',copy:'Most medications can be administered as directed. Please confirm medication needs with the team before the stay and review all instructions at check-in.'},
    {mark:'Comfort',title:'Play, Rest, And Attention',copy:'Guests enjoy supervised indoor and outdoor play, comfortable rest areas, fresh water, and plenty of care and affection throughout the day.'}
  ])}<div class="narrow-panel boarding-inclusions-note"><p><strong>Optional food add-ons:</strong> Food toppers, supplements, and in-house food may be available for an additional fee. Ask the Resort team about the current selection when booking.</p></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Before You Book','Who boarding is for.','All boarding guests must meet Resort daycare requirements.',true)}<div class="narrow-panel">${list(['Social dogs who can participate comfortably in group daycare.','Dogs with a successful Jollytails Resort daycare assessment.','Dogs who have attended Resort daycare or boarding within the past three months.','New guests who complete their assessment at least two weeks before the planned stay.'])}<p>Clients from another Jollytails location still need a Resort profile and assessment because client records and packages are not shared between locations.</p></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container faq-layout"><div>${sectionHead('Boarding FAQs','Everything from sleeping arrangements to booking, pickup, and daily updates.')}</div>${faq([
    {q:'Where does my dog sleep?',html:`<p>Jollytails Resort has several different sleeping arrangements for overnight guests including kennels and crates. Staff select sleeping arrangements based on size (for example, a larger dog has priority over a smaller dog for a kennel) and on where your dog is most comfortable. We very much appreciate insight about your dog’s sleeping habits; for example, if your dog always sleeps in a crate at home then it makes sense for us to continue that at Jollytails Resort.</p>`},
    {q:'Does my dog have to be an existing Jollytails client to board?',html:`<p>It is not necessary to be an existing Jollytails client. Before boarding at the resort, your pooch must complete our daycare social assessment and should attend daycare at least once every three months before a boarding stay at Jollytails Resort. If it has been over three months since we have seen your dog, we will require a reassessment prior to boarding. This helps your pup remain familiar with our facility, staff, and routine between boarding stays.</p>`},
    {q:'How far in advance should I book my dog’s visit?',html:`<p>Reservations are required for all boarding stays. We recommend making your reservations as early as possible to guarantee space for your pup.</p><p>New clients who have not previously stayed at Jollytails Resort are encouraged to make reservations at least two weeks in advance. This will allow time for a social assessment visit for your pup, and a day or two of daycare if needed, prior to their stay.</p><p><strong><em>Unfortunately, we are unable to accommodate last minute and same days reservations for dogs who have not had an assessment visit at Jollytails. Due to staffing requirements for these visits, additional fees may apply for last-minute assessment appointments.</em></strong></p>`},
    {q:'If my dog is currently a client at another Jollytails location, do I need to provide a new assessment form?',html:`<p>Yes. Jollytails Resort does not have access to client information at other Jollytails locations. A new assessment form enables us to create your account at Jollytails Resort and provides us with important, up to date information about your dog. Next steps are determined on a case-by-case basis.</p>`},
    {q:"My dog doesn't get along with other dogs - can you still board them?",html:`<p>Although we offer separate kennels for sleeping, we focus primarily on social activity for dogs. Guests spend their daytime in group play and interaction throughout the day. If your dog does not get along with other dogs, an in-home boarding arrangement may be the best option for you.</p>`},
    {q:'Does my dog need to be spayed/neutered to attend Jollytails Resort? What vaccinations are required?',html:`<p>To stay and play at Jollytails, dogs must be over 16 weeks of age and spayed or neutered (if at least 6 months old). You must provide proof of core vaccines (DHLPP - Distemper, Hepatitis, Leptospirosis, Parvovirus and Parainfluenza as well as Rabies) and a yearly vaccine for Bordetella (canine cough). Your dog must be flea and tick free and must pass our daycare assessment.</p>`},
    {q:'What are your drop-off/pickup time deadlines?',html:`<p>Overnight boarding guests must be dropped off by 1:00 PM on the day their boarding begins so they have lots of time to play with all of their friends before bedtime. If you are unable to drop your pet off by 1:00 PM, please let us know.</p><p>We are open for reserved boarding pickup and 1:00 PM drop-off 365 days a year. Holidays may change pickup and 1:00 PM drop-off procedures, so please ask us for the applicable holiday arrangements.</p><p>The overnight boarding fee includes daycare for the duration of your pup’s stay, including their departure day, until 2:00 PM. Pickups after 2:00 PM will incur additional daycare fees, as per our <a href="/prices">price list</a>.</p>`},
    {q:'What do I need to bring?',html:`<p>If your pet has a favourite bed or blanket, you are welcome to bring it along. You can also bring their favourite toys, bones or chews. You should also ensure that your dog has more than enough of their usual food for their stay at the Resort, as many dogs burn more calories during daycare than they would at home, and can require increased amounts of food to maintain their healthy weight. If your pup eats a type of food that we sell at the Resort, you can purchase a bag here for their stay. The Resort has a dedicated food preparation area that is equipped with a fridge and freezer for raw or other perishable food.</p>`},
    {q:'What can I leave at home?',html:`<p>We ask that you leave any toys with batteries or electronics at home, as well as dishes. Our kitchen is fully stocked with stainless steel food and water bowls, as well as slow-feed dishes.</p>`},
    {q:'What is the latest I can pick up my dog?',html:`<p>You can come in anytime during our regular business hours when our front store is staffed. Please note that we are open for boarding pickup and 1:00 PM drop-off 365 days a year. Holidays may change pickup and 1:00 PM drop-off procedures, so please ask us for the applicable holiday arrangements.</p>`},
    {q:'If you are staffed 24/7, why am I limited to regular business hours to drop off or pick up my dog?',html:`<p>Boarding drop-off is by 1:00 PM. Outside of business hours, Jollytails Resort staff are busy attending to the dogs who are spending the night at the resort. In order to give guests the most attention, resort staff are not able to accommodate pickup outside of the regular hours. If there is a special circumstance or emergency, please let us know and we will do our best to make arrangements.</p>`},
    {q:'What happens if my dog gets sick?',html:`<p>Our first priority is the health and safety of your dog. If at any time our staff feel that your dog requires emergency veterinary care, we will attempt to contact you. If we are unable to reach you or your emergency contact, or if your dog appears to be in immediate distress, we will bring your dog to a veterinary hospital for treatment.</p>`},
    {q:"My dog has special feeding/medication requirements. Can you administer my dog's medications?",html:`<p>Under most circumstances, yes. Please don’t hesitate to ask us about any special requirements for your pet.</p>`},
    {q:'How will I know how my pet is doing?',html:`<p>We send daily report cards by email, letting you know how your dog is doing. Our clients love these updates! The report card includes information on behaviour, play, and other activity. Please note that on Sundays and holidays, you may not receive a report card. You are welcome to contact us to check in on your pup at any time. Our staff will get back to you as quickly as possible.</p>`},
    {q:'How do I book?',html:`<p>New and existing clients can click <a href="/reservations">“Make a Reservation”</a> above and follow the prompts.</p>`},
    {q:'Deposits and Cancellations',html:`<p>The deposit and cancellation policy applies to bookings of 3 nights or greater, as well as to all bookings during these peak periods:</p><ul><li>February Break</li><li>March Break</li><li>Easter Weekend</li><li>Summer Season (June 1 – August 31)</li><li>Holiday Season (December 15 – January 3)</li></ul><p>The boarding deposit is equivalent to one night’s stay (currently $63 plus HST for one pet). Cancellations received seven or more days in advance are eligible for a full refund or credit for future use. Deposits are non-refundable for no-shows and for cancellations later than seven days in advance.</p><p>Deposits during the periods above are non-refundable in the event of cancellation. Bookings for periods of greater than two weeks may require a deposit of 25% of the total. Please contact us for details.</p><p>Early boarding departures may be subject to an early departure charge equal to 50% of the remainder of the stay.</p><p>Our deposit and cancellation policy is subject to change without notice. We will confirm any deposit requirements at the time that you make your reservation.</p>`}
  ])}</div></section>` + cta('Planning a sleepover?','Choose the path that matches whether your dog is new to the Resort or has stayed with us recently.',[requestButton('/reservations/boarding/new','New Guest Request'),reservationButton('/reservations/boarding/existing','Returning Guest Booking')])
});

add('grooming.html', {
  path:'/grooming', title:'Dog Grooming In Bayers Lake', description:'Explore full grooms, baths, nail care, tidy services, and grooming appointment pathways at Jollytails Resort.',
  body: hero({kicker:'Dog Grooming',title:'Patient grooming, tailored to your dog.',copy:'Our grooming team focuses on comfort, safety, and giving each dog the time they need—from a fresh bath and nail trim to a complete groom.',image:img.grooming,alt:'A golden retriever after a grooming appointment at Jollytails Resort',position:'50% 28%',actionsClass:'equal-action-buttons',actions:[requestButton('/reservations/grooming/new','New Client Appointment'),reservationButton('/reservations/grooming/existing','Existing Client Appointment')]}) +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${cards([
    {mark:'Full',title:'Complete Grooming',copy:'Bath, shampoo and conditioner, blow-dry, nails, ear cleaning, and a cut tailored to your dog.'},
    {mark:'Fresh',title:'Bath And Nail Services',copy:'A practical refresh with size-based starting prices for small through giant dogs.'},
    {mark:'Tidy',title:'Finishing Services',copy:'Nails, pads, ears, face trims, clean feet, teeth brushing, and nail Dremel options.'}
  ])}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${split({image:img.grooming2,alt:'A freshly groomed black and white dog standing on a grooming table at Jollytails Resort',kicker:'The Jollytails Resort Difference',title:'Comfort comes first.',body:'<p>We do not rush appointments. Our groomers take the time needed to support a safe, comfortable grooming experience and a result you are happy with, slowing down when a dog needs it.</p><p>Our electric-rise grooming tables have large, non-slip tops that safely accommodate dogs up to 250 pounds. The lift adjusts from 15 to 40 inches, so dogs do not have to jump up or down from a height that could cause injury.</p><p>We use high-quality shampoos, conditioners, wipes, and spritzes made with human-grade ingredients and pure essential oils. They are natural, non-toxic, paraben-free, phthalate-free, and phosphate-free, without artificial colours or fragrances.</p>',reverse:true})}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Complete Grooming Prices','Every service and starting price in one place.','All prices are plus 14% HST. Full-groom prices are estimates; final pricing depends on coat condition, the amount of de-matting required, behaviour, and the requested cut.')}<div class="narrow-panel grooming-service-note"><h3>What a full groom includes</h3><p>A bath, shampoo, conditioner, blow dry, nail clipping, ear cleaning, and hair clipped in the desired cut.</p><p>Groomers assess coat condition before beginning. Dogs with excessive matting require a signed Matted Dog Waiver.</p></div><div class="price-columns grooming-price-grid">${priceTable('Full groom by coat and size',[
    ['Shorthaired small dog · up to 30 lbs','$60.00+'],['Longhaired small dog · up to 30 lbs','$85.00+'],['Shorthaired medium dog · 30–60 lbs','$70.00+'],['Longhaired medium dog · 30–60 lbs','$90.00+'],['Shorthaired large dog · 60+ lbs','$85.00+'],['Longhaired large dog · 60+ lbs','$100.00+']
  ])}${priceTable('Doodle full groom',[
    ['Mini · up to 20 lbs','$100.00+'],['Medium · 20–60 lbs','$110.00+'],['Large · 60–80 lbs','$120.00+'],['Extra large · 80 lbs','$130.00+']
  ])}${priceTable('Tidy-up services',[
    ['Ear cleaning','$10.00'],['Ear cleaning and plucking','$15.00'],['Nails','$15.00'],['Nails and pads','$20.00'],['Pretty feet · shave pads, nail trim, paw-hair trim','$25.00'],['Clean feet and face','$25.00'],['Teeth brushing · with groom or bath','+$5.00'],['Nail Dremel','$5.00 extra'],['Face trim','$15.00+'],['Visor trim','$10.00']
  ])}${priceTable('Bath and nails',[
    ['Small dog · up to 30 lbs','$30.00–$40.00'],['Medium dog · 30–60 lbs','$40.00–$55.00'],['Large dog · 60–90 lbs','$55.00–$70.00'],['Giant dog · 90 lbs and over','$70+']
  ],'The scrubdown service includes a bath, towel dry, and nail trim.')}${priceTable('Sanitary service package',[
    ['Nails, pads, sanitary shave-out, ear cleaning, and visor trim','$40']
  ],'The sanitary package may be accommodated the same day. Please call for availability.')}</div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Appointment Policies','A smoother visit for everyone.')}${list(['Dogs must be picked up within one hour after their appointment is finished. Boarding or daycare fees may apply after that time.','Please provide at least 24 hours’ notice to cancel a grooming appointment.','A $10.00 late-cancellation penalty may apply. Prepayment or a deposit may also be required for the next appointment.','Coat condition, excessive de-matting, behaviour, and the requested cut can affect the final price. A Matted Dog Waiver is required when excessive matting is found.'])}</div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Good to know</p><h2>Anal gland expression is not offered.</h2><p>In Nova Scotia, anal gland expression is considered a medical procedure and can only legally be performed at a veterinary hospital.</p></aside></div></section>` +
  cta('Ready for a fresh start?','Use the appointment path for a new grooming client or a returning grooming client.',[requestButton('/reservations/grooming/new','New Client Request'),reservationButton('/reservations/grooming/existing','Existing Client Request')])
});

add('pet-store.html', {
  path:'/pet-store', title:'Pet Store In Bayers Lake', description:'Shop dry and raw dog food, treats, toys, accessories, and rewards programs at the Jollytails Resort pet store in Halifax.',
  body: hero({kicker:'Jollytails Resort Pet Store',title:'Good food, useful gear, and treats worth sitting for.',copy:'Stop in for dry and raw food, locally made treats, toys, walking gear, enrichment products, and friendly help finding what fits your pet.',image:img.store,alt:'A dog exploring the treat selection inside the Jollytails Resort pet store',actions:[button('/contact','Visit Our Store')]}) +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${sectionHead('More To Browse','A fuller pet-store lineup.','Food is only the beginning. The Resort carries everyday essentials, training favourites, and plenty of things that make life with a pet more fun.',true)}${cards([
    {mark:'Feed',title:'Food, Bowls And Feeders',copy:'Dry, wet, frozen raw, freeze-dried, and dehydrated food, plus toppers, slow-feed bowls, puzzle feeders, and interactive dishes.'},
    {mark:'Treat',title:'Treats, Chews And Rewards',copy:'Training treats, biscuits, long-lasting chews, bully sticks, and options across a wide range of proteins—including hypoallergenic and protein-free choices.'},
    {mark:'Play',title:'Toys And Enrichment',copy:'Fetch, tug, retrieval, plush, durable, food-dispensing, and puzzle toys for physical play, problem-solving, and quieter time at home.'},
    {mark:'Walk',title:'Walking And Training Gear',copy:'Collars, leashes, harnesses, reward pouches, no-pull options, and carefully selected training aids with in-store fitting help.'},
    {mark:'Home',title:'Cleaning And Home Care',copy:'Pet-safe urine and stain removers, enzymatic cleaners, grooming essentials, and practical products for everyday cleanup.'},
    {mark:'Season',title:'Paw And Travel Essentials',copy:'Non-toxic paw protection for ice, snow, and road salt, along with useful accessories for outings and travel.'}
  ])}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${split({image:img.retailFood,alt:'Shelves of dog and cat food available in the Jollytails Resort pet store',kicker:'Food For Every Routine',title:'Compare more than one way to feed.',body:'<p>The store carries food for dogs and cats across a wide range of formats and budgets: frozen raw, freeze-dried and dehydrated raw, dry kibble, canned food, wet food, toppers, broths, and fresh-food additions.</p><p>Choose from meat-forward recipes, limited-ingredient and single-protein diets, grain-inclusive foods, grain-free options, and formulas designed around sensitivities or specific nutritional needs.</p><p>If you are comparing foods because of digestion, stool, skin and coat, weight, ingredients, or simply what your pet enjoys eating, the team can walk you through labels, proteins, formats, and price points.</p>'})}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Frozen, Freeze-Dried And Dehydrated','Raw options for different budgets and routines.','Customers often choose raw for straightforward ingredient lists, meat-forward nutrition, lower-carbohydrate recipes, local sourcing, or simply because their dogs love it.',true)}${brandCards([
    {logo:'/assets/brand-logos/big-country-raw.webp',alt:'Big Country Raw logo',width:'500',height:'416',title:'Big Country Raw',copy:'Canadian frozen raw meals made with carefully selected ingredients, with proteins and formats for dogs and cats.',note:'Resort loyalty offer: Buy 12, Get 1 Free.'},
    {logo:'/assets/brand-logos/primal.webp',alt:'Primal Pet Foods logo',width:'500',height:'219',title:'Primal Pet Foods',copy:'Frozen and freeze-dried recipes, toppers, broths, and fresh-food additions made with high-quality meats, produce, vitamins, and minerals.',note:'Ask the team about current recipes and formats.'}
  ],'brand-grid-featured')}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Quality Dry Food','Reliable favourites for dogs and cats.','Compare established brands in store and ask the team for help narrowing the options for your pet and routine.',true)}${brandCards([
    {logo:'/assets/brand-logos/acana.webp',alt:'Acana pet food logo',width:'360',height:'200',title:'Acana And Orijen',copy:'Canadian-made dog and cat foods with meat-forward recipes using poultry, fish, red meat, eggs, fruits, and vegetables.',note:'Resort loyalty offer: Buy 12 dry-food bags, Get 1 Free.'},
    {logo:'/assets/brand-logos/boreal.webp',alt:'Boréal pet food logo',width:'450',height:'401',title:'Boréal',copy:'Primarily Canadian ingredients, single-source proteins, low-glycemic starches, and simple grain-free wet foods without gums or fillers.',note:'Resort loyalty offer: Buy 12 dry-food bags, Get 1 Free.'},
    {logo:'/assets/brand-logos/go-solutions.webp',alt:'GO! Solutions pet food logo',width:'355',height:'226',title:'GO! Solutions',copy:'Everyday, higher-protein, lower-carbohydrate, and sensitivity-focused recipes using proteins such as chicken, lamb, turkey, salmon, duck, and trout, without by-products, growth hormones, or artificial preservatives.',note:'Resort loyalty offer: Buy 12 dry-food bags, Get 1 Free.'},
    {logo:'/assets/brand-logos/farmina.gif',alt:'Farmina Pet Foods logo',width:'500',height:'414',title:'Farmina',copy:'Dog and cat foods developed around nutrition research, natural antioxidants, non-GMO ingredients, and carefully selected proteins.',note:'Resort loyalty offer: Buy 12 dry-food bags, Get 1 Free.'}
  ])}<div class="narrow-panel pet-store-note"><h3>Lifetime</h3><p>A Canadian-made, single-protein kibble with grain-inclusive recipes and an approachable price point. Lifetime dry food is also included in the Resort’s Buy 12, Get 1 Free program.</p></div><p class="product-availability-note">Brands, recipes, sizes, and stock can change. Call before visiting if you need a specific product.</p></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${split({image:img.retail,alt:'A colourful wall of toys, enrichment products, and walking gear in the Jollytails Resort store',kicker:'Beyond The Bowl',title:'Toys, training tools, and everyday gear.',body:'<p>The store carries practical products for play, enrichment, training, walking, feeding, and care—with help choosing equipment that suits your dog.</p>'+list(['Fetch, tug, chew, plush, and durable toys.','Food-dispensing puzzles, slow feeders, and interactive bowls.','Training treats, reward pouches, and practical training aids.','Collars, harnesses, leashes, and no-pull options.','Cleaners, paw protection, and essentials for home and travel.'])+'<p class="small-note">Confirmed product names include KONG, West Paw, Outward Hound, PetDreamHouse, and FouFit. Selection varies over time.</p>',reverse:true})}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Treats And Enrichment','Turn snacks and meals into something to do.','Dogs are natural foragers. Food-dispensing toys, puzzles, and slow feeders add movement and problem-solving to a daily routine while helping fast eaters slow down.',true)}${cards([
    {mark:'Puzzle',title:'Interactive Feeding',copy:'Slow-feed bowls, puzzle feeders, and sturdy treat dispensers that dogs can shake, roll, or paw to release food.'},
    {mark:'Brands',title:'Favourite Food Toys',copy:'Options from KONG, Outward Hound, West Paw, PetDreamHouse, FouFit, and Nina Ottosson, with choices for different play styles and skill levels.'},
    {mark:'Reward',title:'Training Treats And Chews',copy:'A broad mix of training treats, biscuits, and chews in proteins ranging from beef to crocodile, plus hypoallergenic and protein-free options.'}
  ])}<div class="narrow-panel pet-store-note"><p><strong>Treat brands found in store include:</strong> Crazy Dog, Bare Bones Co., Moose &amp; Maple, My Home Treats, Crumps, Northern, Natural Farm Pets, Nature’s Own, and more.</p></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Specialty Gear And Home Care','Useful solutions for everyday problems.')}<h3>Haqihana harnesses</h3><p>Designed to distribute pressure across the sternum and chest without restricting movement. Two thoughtfully positioned buckles make the harness easier to put on and remove, and the team can help with fit.</p><h3>Urine removers and cleaners</h3><p>Pet-safe options for carpets, upholstery, hardwood, and other surfaces include EnviroFresh cleaners, which use natural ingredients, friendly bacteria, and enzymes to break down urine, organic stains, and proteins.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Cold-Weather Care</p><h2>Protect sensitive paws.</h2><p>Ice, snow, and road salt can quickly irritate paw pads. The store carries safe, non-toxic paw protectors that create a light, breathable barrier for winter walks.</p></aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Choosing A Food','Start with the pet in front of you.')}<p>Quality food matters, but there is no single format that suits every dog or cat. The Resort carries high-meat, limited-ingredient, grain-inclusive, and grain-free foods so customers can compare recipes rather than being pushed toward one approach.</p><p>When reading a label, look at the full recipe and how it fits your pet’s life stage, preferences, sensitivities, and routine—not just the front of the bag. The team has researched the products it stocks and can help explain the differences.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">What To Compare</p><h2>A practical label checklist.</h2>${list(['Named animal proteins rather than vague ingredient descriptions.','A protein, fat, and carbohydrate balance that suits your pet.','Limited-ingredient or single-protein recipes when useful.','Clearly identified fats and oils.','No unnecessary artificial flavours, colours, or preservatives.','Grain-inclusive and grain-free choices based on individual needs.'])}</aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Food Rewards','Buy the food they love. Earn the next one.')}<p>Participating food lines have manufacturer loyalty programs. Ask the team to start or update your card when you shop.</p>${list(['Big Country Raw: Buy 12, Get 1 Free.','Acana and Orijen dry food: Buy 12, Get 1 Free.','Boréal, Farmina, GO!, and Lifetime dry food: Buy 12, Get 1 Free.','HURRAW dehydrated raw: Save 10% when buying four boxes.'])}<p class="small-note">Program terms and eligible products are set by each brand and may change.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">More Ways To Save</p><h2>Retail discounts and rewards.</h2>${list(['Military members and first responders receive 10% off pet retail purchases with identification.','Seniors age 65+ receive 15% off pet retail purchases on the last Thursday of each month.','Retail discounts do not apply to daycare, grooming, boarding, or training services.'])}<p>You can earn Aeroplan miles on purchases at Jollytails. Ask in store for current details.</p></aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Come Browse','Find something your pet will love.')}<p>Stop in to compare food, treats, toys, and gear in person, or call ahead when you are looking for a particular brand, recipe, or size.</p><div class="button-row">${button('tel:+19024448245','Call 902-444-8245')}${button('/contact','Directions And Contact','button-outline')}</div></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Store Hours</p><h2>Open seven days a week.</h2><p>Monday–Friday: 6:30am–7:30pm<br>Saturday: 9am–6pm<br>Sunday: 11am–6pm</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Full Contact Details →</a></aside></div></section>`
});

add('prices.html', {
  path:'/prices', title:'Daycare, Boarding & Grooming Prices', description:'View verified Jollytails Resort daycare packages, boarding rates, grooming starting prices, discounts, and key price policies.',
  body: hero({kicker:'Resort Prices',title:'Clear prices for play, stays, grooming, and more.',copy:'Compare daycare passes, overnight boarding rates, grooming starting prices, and store discounts. All listed prices are before 14% HST unless noted.',image:img.pricesHero,alt:'A happy black and tan dog smiling on the outdoor turf at Jollytails Resort',actions:[button('/reservations','Join Us')]}) +
  `<section class="section" id="daycare"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Doggy Daycare','Single visits and prepaid packages.','Packages are for the Resort location and are not shared with other Jollytails locations.')}<div class="price-columns">${priceTable('One dog',[
    ['Full day','$33.99'],['10 full days','$307'],['20 full days','$575'],['30 full days','$805'],['Partial day · under 4 hours','$24.49'],['10 partial days','$225']
  ])}${priceTable('Multiple dogs from one household',[
    ['Two dogs · full day','$57.49'],['Two dogs · 10 full days','$530'],['Three dogs · full day','$73']
  ])}</div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky" id="boarding"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Overnight Boarding','Per-night rates.','Daycare during the stay is included. Checkout is by 2pm; daycare fees apply after 2pm.')}<div class="price-columns">${priceTable('Boarding',[
    ['One dog','$63/night'],['Two dogs · same household','$116/night'],['Three dogs · same household','$157/night'],['Extended stay · 10+ consecutive days','Contact the Resort']
  ],'Bookings of three days or more require a deposit. Peak-period deposit rules apply.') }<aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Included</p><h3>What the nightly rate covers</h3>${list(['Daycare from check-in through departure day until 2pm.','Private sleeping space and blanket.','Water, feeding, and most medication administration.','Indoor and outdoor play.'])}</aside></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section" id="boarding-policies"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Boarding Deposits And Cancellations','Know the terms before confirming a stay.','These terms apply to bookings of three nights or more and to every booking made for a listed peak period.')}<div class="price-policy-grid"><article class="price-policy-card"><p class="card-tag">Deposits</p><h3>When a deposit is required</h3>${list(['The standard boarding deposit is one night’s stay—currently $63 plus HST for one pet.','Every stay of three nights or longer requires a deposit.','Every booking during a listed peak period requires a deposit, regardless of length.','Stays longer than two weeks may require a deposit equal to 25% of the total booking. Contact the Resort for details.'])}</article><article class="price-policy-card"><p class="card-tag">Peak periods</p><h3>Dates with non-refundable deposits</h3>${list(['February Break.','March Break.','Easter Weekend.','Summer Season: June 1–August 31.','Holiday Season: December 15–January 3.'])}</article><article class="price-policy-card price-policy-card-wide"><p class="card-tag">Changes To A Stay</p><h3>Refunds, credits, no-shows, and early departures</h3>${list(['For a non-peak booking, cancel at least seven days before the stay to receive a full deposit refund or an account credit for future use.','Deposits are non-refundable for no-shows and for non-peak cancellations received fewer than seven days before the stay.','Peak-period deposits are non-refundable if the booking is cancelled.','Leaving boarding early may result in an early-departure charge equal to 50% of the unused remainder of the stay.'])}</article></div><p class="price-policy-footnote">Deposit and cancellation terms may change without notice. The Resort will confirm the applicable deposit and terms when your reservation is made.</p></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section" id="grooming"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Grooming','Starting prices.','Coat condition, size, behaviour, matting, and style determine the final estimate.')}<div class="price-columns">${priceTable('Full grooms',[
    ['Short-haired small · up to 30 lb','$60+'],['Long-haired small · up to 30 lb','$85+'],['Short-haired medium · 30–60 lb','$70+'],['Long-haired medium · 30–60 lb','$90+'],['Short-haired large · 60+ lb','$85+'],['Long-haired large · 60+ lb','$100+']
  ])}${priceTable('Doodles',[
    ['Mini · up to 20 lb','$100+'],['Medium · 20–60 lb','$110+'],['Large · 60–80 lb','$120+'],['Extra large · 80+ lb','$130+']
  ])}${priceTable('Bath and nails',[
    ['Small · up to 30 lb','$30–$40'],['Medium · 30–60 lb','$40–$55'],['Large · 60–90 lb','$55–$70'],['Giant · 90+ lb','$70+']
  ])}${priceTable('Tidy services',[
    ['Ear cleaning','$10'],['Ear cleaning and plucking','$15'],['Nail trim','$15'],['Nails and pads','$20'],['Pretty feet','$25'],['Clean feet and face','$25'],['Face trim','$15+'],['Visor trim','$10'],['Teeth brushing add-on','+$5'],['Nail Dremel add-on','+$5']
  ])}</div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky" id="refunds"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Refunds, Returns And Appointment Cancellations','How refunds are calculated and which purchases qualify.','Keep your receipt, original packaging, and UPC when requesting an eligible product return.')}<div class="price-policy-grid"><article class="price-policy-card"><p class="card-tag">Daycare Packages</p><h3>Unused package value</h3><p>A daycare package refund starts with the amount paid, then subtracts every used day at the full daily rate. A further $50 fee applies to a one-dog 10-day package; a $100 fee applies to every other package. No daycare-package refund is issued after one year of inactivity.</p></article><article class="price-policy-card"><p class="card-tag">Group Training</p><h3>Class deposits and course refunds</h3><p>Class deposits are non-refundable. If you are dissatisfied, the course price—less the deposit—may be refunded at the end of the first class. No refund is issued after attending two or more classes.</p><p class="small-note">Training programs are not currently running; this policy is retained for eligible training purchases covered by the original terms.</p></article><article class="price-policy-card"><p class="card-tag">Food</p><h3>30-day food returns</h3><p>Eligible food purchases may be returned for a full refund within 30 days. Bring back the original bag or frozen box, including its UPC, with at least 50% of the contents remaining.</p></article><article class="price-policy-card"><p class="card-tag">Retail Products</p><h3>10-day product returns</h3><p>Unopened and undamaged collars, toys, harnesses, and other retail products may be returned for a full refund within 10 days. Products damaged through unsupervised use are not eligible for a refund.</p></article><article class="price-policy-card price-policy-card-wide"><p class="card-tag">Grooming Appointments</p><h3>Cancellations and pickup</h3>${list(['Provide at least 24 hours’ notice to cancel or reschedule a grooming appointment.','A $10 late-cancellation fee may apply when sufficient notice is not provided.','Prepayment or a deposit may be required for the next appointment.','Pick up your dog within one hour after the appointment is finished. Regular daycare or boarding fees may apply after that time.'])}</article></div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section" id="late-pickup"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Daycare Late Pickup Fees','After the daycare closing time.','Once daycare closes, staff need to prepare meals and settle overnight guests. Late-pickup fees help protect that care time, and all fees collected are donated to the Nova Scotia SPCA.')}<p>If you expect to be delayed, contact the Resort as soon as possible. If the team cannot reach you or your emergency contacts after 30 minutes, your dog will be boarded safely.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Late Fee Schedule</p><h2>Fees after closing</h2>${list(['Up to 15 minutes late: $10.','15–30 minutes late: $15.','More than 30 minutes late: regular boarding rates plus daycare fees apply if neither you nor your emergency contacts can be reached.'])}</aside></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-cream" id="discounts"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Pet Store Discounts','For eligible retail purchases.')}${list(['Military and first responders: 10% off pet retail purchases with identification.','Seniors age 65+: 15% off pet retail purchases on the last Thursday of each month.'])}</div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Please note</p><h2>Retail only.</h2><p>These discounts do not apply to daycare, grooming, boarding, or training services.</p></aside></div></section>` + cta('Ready to choose a service?','Start at the reservation hub for the correct new-client or returning-client path.',[button('/reservations','Reservation Options','button-light')])
});

add('about.html', {
  path:'/about', title:'About Jollytails Resort', description:'Get to know the locally owned and operated Jollytails Resort facility in Bayers Lake, Halifax.',
  body: hero({kicker:'About The Resort',title:'Built around active days and comfortable stays.',copy:'Jollytails Resort is locally owned and operated in Bayers Lake, bringing daycare, overnight boarding, grooming, and pet supplies together under one roof.',image:img.aboutSign,alt:'Jollytails Resort sign at 15 McQuade Lake Crescent in Bayers Lake',position:'50% 45%',actions:[button('/contact','Visit The Resort')]}) +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${split({image:img.beds,alt:'Dogs gathered on raised resting beds inside the Resort',kicker:'The Facility',title:'Room to play, rest, and settle in.',imageClass:'about-facility-image',body:'<p>Spacious indoor and outdoor play areas give social dogs room to move and take breaks. Turf play yards, climate-controlled indoor rooms, and private overnight sleeping spaces support the different rhythms of a daycare day or boarding stay.</p><p>The team is on site 24 hours a day when boarding guests are staying with us.</p>'})}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Under One Roof','A simpler routine for dogs and their people.', '', true)}${cards([
    {mark:'Play',title:'Daycare',copy:'Supervised social play with groups selected for size, comfort, and play style.'},
    {mark:'Stay',title:'Boarding',copy:'Daytime play, private sleeping arrangements, and overnight staff on site.'},
    {mark:'Fresh',title:'Grooming',copy:'Patient, comfort-focused appointments for baths, trims, nails, and complete grooms.'},
    {mark:'Shop',title:'Pet Store',copy:'Food, treats, toys, enrichment, walking gear, and practical help in one convenient stop.'}
  ])}</div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container content-two-col"><div>${sectionHead('Locally Owned And Operated','Your Bayers Lake Jollytails.') }<p>Jollytails Resort is part of the broader Jollytails family, bringing the familiar Jollytails approach to friendly service, supervised social care, and practical support into its Bayers Lake location. The Resort is locally owned and operated, with its own team and service details, and adds overnight boarding to daycare, grooming, and pet retail under one roof.</p><p>Our team is here to make every visit comfortable for your dog and simpler for you. Whether your dog is here for a few hours, a fresh groom, or a longer stay, we focus on clear communication and care that fits the individual dog.</p></div><aside class="callout-card"><p class="card-tag">Find Us</p><h2>15 McQuade Lake Crescent</h2><p>Halifax, Nova Scotia<br>B3S 1C4</p><p>Across from the Coastal Inn and around the corner from the Halifax Tower Hotel.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Hours, Directions And Contact →</a></aside></div></section>` + cta('Come see what the Resort offers.','Contact the team with questions about your dog or plan a visit to the Resort.',[button('/contact','Contact Us','button-light')])
});

add('team.html', {
  path:'/team', title:'Meet The Jollytails Resort Team', description:'Meet the current retail, daycare, boarding, and grooming team at Jollytails Resort in Bayers Lake.',
  body: hero({kicker:'Meet The Team',title:'The people behind every play day, sleepover, and fresh groom.',copy:'Our team brings together Resort operations, pet retail, supervised daycare and boarding, and professional grooming.',image:img.teamHero,alt:'Three dogs playing together in the snowy outdoor turf yard at Jollytails Resort',position:'50% 50%'}) +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Resort Leadership And Retail','The team welcoming pets and people.')}<div class="team-grid">${[
    ['Stephanie West','Resort Manager'],['Sasha D’Entremont','Resort Assistant Manager'],['Tori Gavel','Retail Specialist'],['Taya Weeks-Williams','Retail Specialist']
  ].map(x=>`<article class="team-card"><div class="team-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>${x[0].split(' ').map(n=>n[0]).join('').slice(0,2)}</span></div><h3>${x[0]}</h3><p>${x[1]}</p></article>`).join('')}</div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section section-sky"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Daycare And Boarding','Supervising active days and comfortable stays.')}<div class="team-grid team-grid-compact">${[
    ['Jordan Gilmer','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Supervisor'],['Makenna Slaunwhite','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Supervisor'],['Annalise Crossman','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Faith Rose','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Amanda Ballesteros-Emberly','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Jayla Elizabeth','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Paityn McCormick','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Peter Lutz','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Emma Jarvis','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Herve Kazungu','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Vicky Greer','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant'],['Jack Sampson','Doggy Daycare And Boarding Attendant']
  ].map(x=>`<article class="team-card"><div class="team-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>${x[0].split(' ').map(n=>n[0]).join('').slice(0,2)}</span></div><h3>${x[0]}</h3><p>${x[1]}</p></article>`).join('')}</div></div></section>` +
  `<section class="section"><div class="container">${sectionHead('Grooming','Comfort-focused care from bath to finish.')}<div class="team-grid"><article class="team-card"><div class="team-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>MS</span></div><h3>Meghan Smith</h3><p>Groomer</p></article><article class="team-card"><div class="team-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>CH</span></div><h3>Caitlin Harvie</h3><p>Groomer</p></article><article class="team-card team-card-mascot"><div class="team-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>🐾</span></div><h3>Flurry The Cattle Dog</h3><p>Boss Lady</p></article></div></div></section>` + cta('Interested in joining the team?','See current opportunities and learn how to apply.',[button('/careers','Explore Careers','button-light')])
});

